Cookie that is being used takes an array in php, json_encodes it, xor encrypts it, then base64encodes it.
The default cookie value is taken from an initial request.  Since the PHP gives us the plaintext values that
were used to generate this cookie, we can then produce the input just before the xor_encrypt and the output
right after it.  (initial plaintext=>json_encode to get the former, initial cookie=>base64_decode to get the
latter).  When you xor these two values, a repeating sequence of the key used to encrypt is produced.  After
getting this key, simply change the initial plaintext to set showpassword to "yes", then create your own cookie
that gets you in.  Note that you must tweak xor_encrypt a bit to do the deed.

